WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
Разница между “I like” и “I’d like”.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.200 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
Many learners confuse “I like” and “I’d like”.
They’re not the same.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.900 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
“I like coffee” means coffee is something you enjoy in general.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:19.700 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
But “I’d like a coffee” means you want a coffee right now.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:25.600 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
So in a cafe, don’t say “I like a coffee”.
Say: “I’d like a coffee, please.”

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.700 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
“I like” - generally. “I’d like” - I want it right now.
